--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Panoptes builds on the following open-source software. Base dependencies
(installed with every build):

  * NumPy (BSD-3-Clause), opencv-python-headless (Apache-2.0 Python
    bindings; the prebuilt wheels bundle FFmpeg (LGPL) and, on some
    platforms, GPL-licensed x264/x265 object code — see docs/LICENSING.md),
    Pydantic + pydantic-settings (MIT), PyYAML (MIT), FastAPI (MIT),
    Starlette (BSD-3-Clause), Uvicorn (BSD-3-Clause), python-multipart
    (Apache-2.0), SQLAlchemy (MIT), aiosqlite (MIT), Alembic (MIT),
    httpx (BSD-3-Clause), Typer (MIT), structlog (Apache-2.0/MIT),
    prometheus-client (Apache-2.0).
  * uvicorn[standard] runtime companions: uvloop (MIT/Apache-2.0),
    httptools (MIT), websockets (BSD-3-Clause), watchfiles (MIT),
    python-dotenv (BSD-3-Clause).

Optional extras (installed only when explicitly selected):

  * ultralytics / YOLO26 ("yolo" extra) — AGPL-3.0, including model
    weights. Not included in default builds; commercial redistribution
    requires an Ultralytics Enterprise License or full AGPL compliance.
  * rfdetr ("rfdetr" extra) — Apache-2.0 code; Nano/Small/Medium/Large
    weights are Apache-2.0 (XL/2XL tiers are under a different license
    and are not used by Panoptes).
  * onnxruntime ("onnx" extra) — MIT.
  * fast-plate-ocr and open-image-models ("alpr" extra) — MIT. See
    docs/LICENSING.md for the provenance note on the bundled
    plate-detector weights.
  * PyAV ("av" extra) — BSD-3-Clause bindings; prebuilt wheels bundle
    FFmpeg with GPL-licensed x264/x265. See docs/LICENSING.md before
    redistributing container images that include this extra.
  * asyncpg ("postgres" extra) — Apache-2.0.
  * nvidia-ml-py ("gpu-monitor" extra) — BSD-3-Clause.

The ByteTrack-style tracker in panoptes.track is a clean-room
implementation of the published algorithm; it contains no code from the
original ByteTrack repository or from any AGPL-licensed tracker package.

Full licensing analysis, including model-weight provenance and the CI
license gate, is documented in docs/LICENSING.md.
